{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-ghost-playback-014-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/GhostMapObservabilityTests.cs", "line": 561, "method": "Builder_NewDecisionFields_DefaultsRecordingIndexToZero_NoLeakageInProductionLines", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostMapPresence.Observability.cs:63; add RecordingIndex = -1 to the NewDecisionFields initializer -> red", "what_it_asserts": "NewDecisionFields(\"source-resolve\").RecordingIndex equals 0.", "why_weak": "The name promises no idx leakage in production lines, but no production emit path is driven and no line is built. It pins the struct default that the leak came from, so the sensible hardening (default the field to the -1 unknown sentinel at GhostMapPresence.Observability.cs:63) reds it while the actual leak class stays uncovered.", "proposed_action": "Rename to state what it pins (the NaN/zero sentinel contract of NewDecisionFields), and cover the real claim with a cell that drives EmitSourceResolveLine (GhostMapPresence.cs:4407) with a known index and asserts the emitted line carries it.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "GhostMapPresence", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/GhostMapPresence.cs", "sut_line": 4407, "case_kind": "integration", "proposed_name": "EmitSourceResolveLine_PopulatesIndexBranchAndBodyFromItsArguments", "sketch": "Drive EmitSourceResolveLine (or the smallest production wrapper reachable headless) with recordingIndex 7 and a state-vector source, capture the log sink, and assert the emitted line carries idx=7, source=, body= and the state-vector numerics. The two DecisionLine cells at GhostMapObservabilityTests.cs:411 and :466 build their field structs by hand, so no test covers the production population step.", "guards": "A production emit path that forgets to set a field (the exact #547 idx=0 defect) currently reds nothing.", "risk": "playback"}
